{"content_hash": "f986a9d014d3693b", "version_id": 663, "article_id": 67, "level_code": "en_b1", "lang": "en", "level": 3, "level_label": "B1 中级", "title": "Bank of America fined $1.2bn over money-laundering failures", "title_zh": "美国银行因反洗钱失职被罚12亿美元", "has_translation": true, "topic": "business", "source": "guardian_business", "source_url": "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/oct/14/bank-of-america-fined-money-laundering", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1527874594978-ee4f8a05b4c1?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8MXx8YmFuayUyMGFtZXJpY2ElMjBmaW5lZHxlbnwwfDB8fHwxNzkyMDIyNTY4fDA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Melinda Gimpel on Unsplash", "author": "Melinda Gimpel", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@melindagimpel?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/petition-to-file-for-bankruptcy-9j8k3l9afkc?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(122, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(160, 46%, 48%)", "label": "BUSINESS", "seed": "04b2441ba82d"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-15", "word_count": 173, "reading_minutes": 0.9, "lead": "US regulators have fined Bank of America $1.21bn for failing to detect possible money laundering. The bank says the penalty will hurt its third-quarter earnings.", "lead_zh": "美国监管机构对美国银行开出12.1亿美元罚单，原因是该行未能发现可能的洗钱活动。银行表示，这笔罚款将影响其第三季度盈利。", "preview": "The US Treasury said the fine is the third-largest in its history. Bank of America failed to report more than $5bn in suspicious activity, a", "preview_zh": "美国财政部表示，这是其历史上第三大罚单。美国银行未能报告超过50亿美元的可疑活动，其中10亿美元涉及国家安全风险。财政部长斯科特·贝森特表示，银行必须保护美国金融体系。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 652, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/67/en_b1.mp3", "duration": 74.2, "size_bytes": 446112, "engine": "kokoro", "voice": "af_heart", "word_count": 203, "has_timeline": true, "alternates": [{"voice": "af_bella", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/67/en_b1_af_bella.mp3", "duration": 75.375, "size_bytes": 453168, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 203, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/67/en_b1_af_bella.json"}, {"voice": "am_michael", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/67/en_b1_am_michael.mp3", "duration": 79.3, "size_bytes": 476784, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 203, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/67/en_b1_am_michael.json"}, {"voice": "bf_emma", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/67/en_b1_bf_emma.mp3", "duration": 68.275, "size_bytes": 410544, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 203, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/67/en_b1_bf_emma.json"}, {"voice": "bm_george", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/67/en_b1_bm_george.mp3", "duration": 75.625, "size_bytes": 454752, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 203, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/67/en_b1_bm_george.json"}]}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@77e69fb/content/data/versions/663.json", "paragraphs": ["The US Treasury said the fine is the third-largest in its history. Bank of America failed to report more than $5bn in suspicious activity, although $1bn of that involved national security risks. Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent said banks must protect the US financial system.", "The Treasury added that the bank focused too much on revenue and relied on outside warnings instead of its own controls. Under the order, Bank of America must hire an independent party to review past transactions and report anything suspicious to the government.", "A bank spokesperson said it has invested billions in technology and thousands of employees to fight financial crime. However, the bank will record a $1.2bn charge, which cuts quarterly net income by about 17 cents a share. Shares fell 2.7% after hours.", "The fine includes a $750m civil penalty from the Office of the Comptroller of the Currency, its largest ever. The bank also paid $11.6m for over 400 sanctions violations, including payments linked to Russia and Iran. This follows a $350m fine for American Express."], "paragraphs_zh": ["美国财政部表示，这是其历史上第三大罚单。美国银行未能报告超过50亿美元的可疑活动，其中10亿美元涉及国家安全风险。财政部长斯科特·贝森特表示，银行必须保护美国金融体系。", "财政部还指出，该行过于注重收入，并依赖外部警告，而不是自己的管控。根据命令，美国银行必须聘请独立第三方审查过去的交易，并向政府报告任何可疑情况。", "银行发言人表示，已投入数十亿美元和数千名员工打击金融犯罪。然而，银行将计入12亿美元的支出，这将使季度净利润每股减少约17美分。盘后股价下跌2.7%。", "罚款包括货币监理署开出的7.5亿美元民事罚款，这是该机构史上最大罚单。银行还因400多项制裁违规支付了1160万美元，其中包括与俄罗斯和伊朗有关的付款。此前，美国运通也被罚款3.5亿美元。"], "body": "The US Treasury said the fine is the third-largest in its history. Bank of America failed to report more than $5bn in suspicious activity, although $1bn of that involved national security risks. Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent said banks must protect the US financial system.\n\nThe Treasury added that the bank focused too much on revenue and relied on outside warnings instead of its own controls. Under the order, Bank of America must hire an independent party to review past transactions and report anything suspicious to the government.\n\nA bank spokesperson said it has invested billions in technology and thousands of employees to fight financial crime. However, the bank will record a $1.2bn charge, which cuts quarterly net income by about 17 cents a share. Shares fell 2.7% after hours.\n\nThe fine includes a $750m civil penalty from the Office of the Comptroller of the Currency, its largest ever. The bank also paid $11.6m for over 400 sanctions violations, including payments linked to Russia and Iran. This follows a $350m fine for American Express.", "body_zh": "美国财政部表示，这是其历史上第三大罚单。美国银行未能报告超过50亿美元的可疑活动，其中10亿美元涉及国家安全风险。财政部长斯科特·贝森特表示，银行必须保护美国金融体系。\n\n财政部还指出，该行过于注重收入，并依赖外部警告，而不是自己的管控。根据命令，美国银行必须聘请独立第三方审查过去的交易，并向政府报告任何可疑情况。\n\n银行发言人表示，已投入数十亿美元和数千名员工打击金融犯罪。然而，银行将计入12亿美元的支出，这将使季度净利润每股减少约17美分。盘后股价下跌2.7%。\n\n罚款包括货币监理署开出的7.5亿美元民事罚款，这是该机构史上最大罚单。银行还因400多项制裁违规支付了1160万美元，其中包括与俄罗斯和伊朗有关的付款。此前，美国运通也被罚款3.5亿美元。", "text": "The US Treasury said the fine is the third-largest in its history. Bank of America failed to report more than $5bn in suspicious activity, although $1bn of that involved national security risks. Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent said banks must protect the US financial system. The Treasury added that the bank focused too much on revenue and relied on outside warnings instead of its own controls. Under the order, Bank of America must hire an independent party to review past transactions and report anything suspicious to the government. A bank spokesperson said it has invested billions in technology and thousands of employees to fight financial crime. However, the bank will record a $1.2bn charge, which cuts quarterly net income by about 17 cents a share. Shares fell 2.7% after hours. The fine includes a $750m civil penalty from the Office of the Comptroller of the Currency, its largest ever. The bank also paid $11.6m for over 400 sanctions violations, including payments linked to Russia and Iran. This follows a $350m fine for American Express.", "vocab": [{"word": "fine", "pos": "noun", "zh": "罚款", "note": "常用搭配：be fined for... 因……被罚款", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "money laundering", "pos": "noun", "zh": "洗钱", "note": "指将非法资金合法化的行为", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "suspicious", "pos": "adj", "zh": "可疑的", "note": "suspicious activity 可疑活动", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "regulator", "pos": "noun", "zh": "监管机构", "note": "如 US regulators 美国监管机构", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "penalty", "pos": "noun", "zh": "处罚，罚款", "note": "可数名词，常与 pay 连用", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "earnings", "pos": "noun", "zh": "收益，盈利", "note": "常用复数，如 quarterly earnings 季度收益", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "compliance", "pos": "noun", "zh": "合规", "note": "指遵守法律和规定", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "transaction", "pos": "noun", "zh": "交易", "note": "如 bank transactions 银行交易", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "sanction", "pos": "noun", "zh": "制裁", "note": "常用复数 sanctions，如 sanctions programs 制裁项目", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "share", "pos": "noun", "zh": "股票，股份", "note": "如 shares fell 股价下跌", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "title_original": "Bank of America fined $1.2bn for money-laundering failures", "summary_original": "Third-largest fine in US treasury’s history, due to failure to report suspicious activity, may affect third-quarter earnings\nBank of America\n(BAC.N), has been fined $1.21bn by US regulators for widespread failures to detect ‌potential money laundering and other illicit activity, a penalty the bank said will hurt third-quarter earnings.\nThe US treasury department said the fine, the third-largest in department history, is due to the bank’s failure to report more than $5bn in suspicious activity to the government, including $1bn that posed national security-related and other priority illicit finance risks.\nContinue reading...", "body_original": "Bank of America fined $1.2bn for money-laundering failures\nThird-largest fine in US treasury’s history, due to failure to report suspicious activity, may affect third-quarter earnings\nBank of America\n(BAC.N), has been fined $1.21bn by US regulators for widespread failures to detect ‌potential money laundering and other illicit activity, a penalty the bank said will hurt third-quarter earnings.\nThe US treasury department said the fine, the third-largest in department history, is due to the bank’s failure to report more than $5bn in suspicious activity to the government, including $1bn that posed national security-related and other priority illicit finance risks.\n“Financial institutions are on the ​front lines of protecting our economic and national security,” the treasury secretary, Scott Bessent, said in a statement. “When a bank of this size ​fails to meet its anti-money laundering and sanctions obligations, the consequences extend far beyond its own walls, exposing the ⁠entire US financial system to significant illicit finance risks.”\nThe treasury said the bank “prioritized its revenues” in building compliance programs, and overly relied on inquiries ​from outside parties such as law enforcement and other financial institutions instead of its own internal controls.\nThe consent order requires\nBank of America\nto hire an ​independent third party to review past transactions, identify suspicious activity that the bank failed to detect at the time and report those transactions to the treasury department’s Financial Crimes Enforcement Network.\n“Financial crime compliance is serious, and we are responsible for getting it right,” said a Bank of America spokesperson in a statement. “We have invested billions of dollars in technology and dedicated thousands of ​employees to combat financial crime, and our team is far along with and committed to completing the work required to address the issues raised ​by our regulators.”\nThe spokesperson added that the bank’s third-quarter results due for release on Wednesday would include a non-tax-deductible charge of $1.2bn, which will reduce quarterly net income ‌by approximately ⁠17 cents a share.\nAnalysts have estimated adjusted earnings per share of $1.10, according to mean estimates compiled by LSEG, but that excludes one-offs like this fine.\nShares were down 2.7% in after-hours trading after closing the day down 1.1%.\nThe penalty is likely to add to negative investor sentiment and raise concerns about higher expenses and whether Bank of America can maintain its roughly $6bn quarterly share buyback pace, the UBS analyst Erika Najarian said in a note.\nWith earnings due ​on Wednesday, “we think shares likely underperforming at ​open”, she said.\nShe noted there ⁠was no asset cap, a regulatory penalty that would limit how large the bank could grow.\nAs part of the fine, the treasury department’s office of the comptroller of the currency levied a $750m civil ​penalty against the lender, the largest ever for the regulator, citing failures to address shortcomings in its anti-money ​laundering programs that were ⁠identified as part of a 2024 cease-and-desist order from the watchdog.\nThe regulator said the bank’s compliance program was “deficient and ineffective”, and its transaction monitoring system caused the bank to delay filing suspicious activity reports on billions of dollars of transactions.\nIn addition, the bank paid an $11.6m fine to the treasury department’s office of foreign ⁠assets control ​for more than 400 apparent violations of numerous sanctions programs. The treasury said the bank mistakenly ​processed millions of dollars in payments that violated sanctions programs targeting countries including Russia and Iran.\nThe fine comes days after American Express\nwas also hit with a $350m penalty\nfor similar anti-money ​laundering shortcomings.\nExplore more on these topics\nBank of America\nBanking\nRegulators\nnews\nShare\nReuse this content", "fetched_at": "2026-10-15T00:02:46.794735", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "The", "s": 0.275, "e": 0.388, "sm": 275, "em": 387, "cs": 0, "ce": 3, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "US", "s": 0.388, "e": 0.75, "sm": 387, "em": 750, "cs": 4, "ce": 6, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "Treasury", "s": 0.75, "e": 1.25, "sm": 750, "em": 1250, "cs": 7, "ce": 15, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "said", "s": 1.25, "e": 1.387, "sm": 1250, "em": 1387, "cs": 16, "ce": 20, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "the", "s": 1.387, "e": 1.488, "sm": 1387, "em": 1487, "cs": 21, "ce": 24, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "fine", "s": 1.488, "e": 1.875, "sm": 1487, "em": 1874, "cs": 25, "ce": 29, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "is", "s": 1.875, "e": 2.025, "sm": 1875, "em": 2024, "cs": 30, "ce": 32, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "the", "s": 2.025, "e": 2.175, "sm": 2025, "em": 2